{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">AND operator (bitwise)</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/308867","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/AND-operator-bitwise.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/AND-operator-bitwise.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"AND-operator-bitwise\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">AND operator (bitwise)</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Performs a bitwise AND operation on two expressions of the same flag enum type and returns\n        a new instance of the same type.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d404529e96\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><var class=\"keyword varname\">flag-enum-expression</var> AND <var class=\"keyword varname\">flag-enum-expression</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\"><var class=\"keyword varname\">flag-enum-expression</var></dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression whose value is a flag enum instance. Both expressions must be the same\n            flag enum type, and neither expression can be the Unknown value\n            (<code class=\"ph codeph\">?</code>).</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"AND-operator-bitwise__example_GC153O2679538\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d404529e142\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">You can use bitwise AND to check to see if a particular flag or flags is set. This code\n        fragment defines a variable of type <code class=\"ph codeph\">Progress.Reflect.Flags</code> (see the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Progress.Reflect.Flags-enumeration.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Progress.Reflect.Flags-enumeration.html\">Progress.Reflect.Flags enumeration</a> entry for a full list of members) and uses AND\n        to check to see if the <code class=\"ph codeph\">Public</code> flag is set.</p>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"AND-operator-bitwise__idGDN2OG2673595\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE flagsEnum AS Progress.Reflect.Flags.\n\nflagsEnum = Flags:Public OR Flags:Private.\n \nIF (flagsEnum AND Flags:Public) EQ Flags:Public THEN...</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <p class=\"p\">The bitwise AND operation results in an enum instance in which the only flags set are the\n        flags set in both expressions. In this case, the resulting instance has the\n          <code class=\"ph codeph\">Public</code> flag set.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">You can also use <code class=\"ph codeph\">Progress.Lang.FlagsEnum</code>&#39;s <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"IsFlagSet-method.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/IsFlagSet-method.html\">IsFlagSet( ) method</a> to achieve the same result:</p>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>IF flagsEnum:IsFlagSet(Flags:Public) THEN...</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d404529e218\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\"><li class=\"li\">This operator can be used with both ABL and .NET flag enums.</li></ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"AND-operator-bitwise__see-also_GC153P2679542\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d404529e228\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\"><a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ENUM-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ENUM-statement.html\">ENUM statement</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"IsFlagSet-method.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/IsFlagSet-method.html\">IsFlagSet( ) method</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"NOT-operator-bitwise.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/NOT-operator-bitwise.html\">NOT operator (bitwise)</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"XOR-operator-bitwise.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/XOR-operator-bitwise.html\">XOR operator (bitwise)</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OR-operator-bitwise.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OR-operator-bitwise.html\">OR operator (bitwise)</a></p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"AMBIGUOUS-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/AMBIGUOUS-function.html\">AMBIGUOUS function</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"AND-operator-logical.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/AND-operator-logical.html\">AND operator (logical)</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/308867","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1470,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"AND operator (bitwise)","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/AND-operator-bitwise.html","type":"Manual"}